<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Florence</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Florence is a city in Tuscany, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and a leading centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a>. Byzantine émigré scholars contributed greatly to the revival of Greek learning there, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-florence">Council of Florence</a> (1438–1445) sought to reunite the Byzantine and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> churches in the last years of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florence.jpg" alt="Florence" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giorgio Galeotti · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Firenze_-_Piazzale_Michelangelo,_Firenze,_Italy_-_April_6,_2015_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
